    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμμεμᾰώς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υῖα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in eager haste, eager</i>, of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.142
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.619e
			</span></i>, etc.; of things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχή</span> (or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρη</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				439
			</span></i>: later c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμμεμαὼς Βέβρυξι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.121
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μάω,
			μέμονα</span>.)</div>
